 "notes": "Limit on axion-electron coupling |g_p| from a radiofrequency fermionic (spin-resonance) interferometer haloscope. g_p is defined in Eq.(1) via L=(g_p/2m_f) psibar gamma_mu gamma5 d^mu a psi with m_f=m_e, which is exactly the canonical g_ae=C_e m_e/f_a, so no conversion needed. Curve traced from Fig.5 (paper.pdf v2), the green 'This work' excluded region; the reported limit is its lower (spiky, broadband) boundary, from ~1e-11 eV to 3.6e-10 eV. Minimum |g_p|=1.2e-7 at m_a~0.36 neV matches the extracted curve (1.20e-7 at 3.56e-10 eV). Vector calibration: x-frame [97.28,294.40]px->[1e-11,1e-8]eV, y-frame [59.93,187.50]px->[1e-1,1e-26]. Paper states 2sigma=90% C.L. Assumed local DM density rho_dm=0.4 GeV/cm^3 (page 1); not rescaled. NOTE: a later arXiv version (95% C.L., mass extended to 1e-9 eV) exists; reported here is the v2 headline curve matching the supplied PDF.",
